# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  הכסף שלנו — what does NOT belong in the repository
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The ministries' spreadsheets are BUILD INPUTS, not source. The workflow
# caches them between runs; 82 files a quarter in git history would bloat the
# repo forever to store something we can re-download in a minute.
reports/*.xlsx
reports/manifest.json

# a stray copy in the project root — it belongs in reports\
/repository-of-answers_*.xlsx

# the raw contract_spending pull. Also a build input: hundreds of MB of the
# same rows the API will hand us again next month.
build/

# LibreOffice / Excel leave these behind while a file is open
.~lock.*#
~$*
*.tmp

# node
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# python leaves these next to any module it imports — the test runs on GitHub
# will make tools/__pycache__ every time
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# leftovers from tidy-up.bat / clean-up-2.bat
_old_delete_me/
*.log

# downloaded Actions artifacts and the locally built databases — the inputs
# and outputs of build-database.bat (added 2026-08-25). Hundreds of MB, all
# reproducible: artifacts re-download from Actions, the databases rebuild
# in one click.
/full-records.zip
/budgetkey-raw.zip
/portal-registers.zip
/publications-register.zip
/contracts.db
/contracts-public.db

# NOTE: site/data/**  IS committed on purpose. Those JSON files are what the
# site actually reads, and what the monthly workflow updates. That is the
# point of putting this on GitHub.
#
# WITH ONE EXCEPTION, added 2026-08-23 after the first full run.
# The .full.json files — every column of every row — came to 241 MB across 49
# sections, with 0024.full.json alone at 33.7 MB. GitHub's recommended maximum
# file size is 1 MB (enforced at 100 MB) and 28 of them are over it. They are
# rewritten every month, so each refresh would add another 241 MB to history
# forever. The lean files the site actually loads are 7.6 MB for all 49.
# The full files are still produced and still downloadable — the workflow
# uploads them as a build artifact. They just do not live in git.
site/data/paid/*.full.json

# raw register exports from mr.gov.il (Mercy downloads them by hand - the
# portal does not serve robots) and the JSON they convert to. Hundreds of MB;
# they live on disk, never in git history.
/Exemptions-*/
/Tenders-*/
